-- title:
--   Special fibre of X₀(N₀) over a place above q
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0 \ge 1$ and a prime $q$ with $q \nmid N_0$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ belongs to the nonunits of $A$, whose residue field $\kappa_A$ has characteristic $q$ and is algebraically closed, and let $\rho \colon \mathrm{DRLevel.R}\,q \to A$ be a ring homomorphism (the base ring being [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt q`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8)) whose composite with the inclusion $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ is the structural map of $\mathrm{DRLevel.R}\,q$. Write $\kappa_A(j,j_{N_0})$ for `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa_A\,N_0$, the subfield of $\kappa_A$-Laurent series generated by `jqModC` $\kappa_A$ and its $N_0$-fold $q$-substitution `jqNModC`. Then there exist a `CurveModel` $M$ of $\kappa_A(j,j_{N_0})$ over $\kappa_A$ — an integral scheme $M.C$, proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\kappa_A$, with a ring isomorphism $M.\mathrm{ffEquiv}$ of $\kappa_A(j,j_{N_0})$ onto the function field of $M.C$ over $\kappa_A$, a bijection of its closed points onto the places of $\kappa_A(j,j_{N_0})$ over $\kappa_A$ matching stalks with valuation rings, and the property that every finite subset lies in an affine open — and an isomorphism $e \colon M.C \to \mathrm{fibre0}\,((\mathrm{residue}\,A) \circ \rho)$, the base change of the Igusa scheme structure morphism $\mathrm{toBase0}\,N_0\,q$ along $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $\mathrm{DRLevel.R}\,q \to \kappa_A$, such that: the preimage under $e$ followed by the first projection of the open image of the finite chart $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}\,N_0\,q$ is non-empty; $e$ followed by the second projection equals $M.\mathrm{toBase}$, so $e$ is a morphism over $\kappa_A$; and for every $b$ in the finite chart algebra `chartAlgFin` $N_0\,q$, letting $\mathrm{read}\,b \in \kappa_A(j,j_{N_0})$ be the element obtained by pulling $b$ back along $e$ followed by the first projection over that chart open, taking the germ at the generic point, and transporting through $M.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$, one has $\mathrm{read}\,b =$ `jGeomGen` $\kappa_A\,N_0$ whenever $b =$ `jChartFin` $N_0\,q$, and $\mathrm{read}\,b =$ `jNGeomGen` $\kappa_A\,N_0$ whenever the Laurent series underlying $b$ is $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb Q\,N_0\,j$.
--
--   This is the characteristic-$q$ dictionary for the Igusa/Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(N_0)$ at a place of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ above a prime $q \nmid N_0$: it identifies the fibre with a smooth proper model of the modular function field in characteristic $q$ and pins down the images of the two distinguished chart generators. It is the place-by-place input to [`ModularCurve.DRLevel.exists_curveModel_iso_fibre0_chartPin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRLevel.exists_curveModel_iso_fibre0_chartPin), which supplies the special-fibre data of the Deligne–Rapoport level-$N_0q$ package.
